question:
Calculate the critical angle for total internal reflection of light traveling between the following media:
(1) from glass to air;
(2) from water to air;
(3) from glass to water.

solution:
Solution: Assume the refractive indices of air, water, and glass are $n_{1}=1.000, n_{2}=1.333$, $n_{3}=1.516$, then:

$$
\begin{aligned}
& i_{1 c}=\arcsin \frac{n_{1}}{n_{3}}=\arcsin \frac{1.000}{1.516}=41^{\circ} 16^{\prime} \\
& i_{2 c}=\arcsin \frac{n_{1}}{n_{2}}=\arcsin \frac{1.000}{1.333}=48^{\circ} 36^{\prime} \\
& i_{3 c}=\arcsin \frac{n_{2}}{n_{3}}=\arcsin \frac{1.333}{1.516}=61^{\circ} 33^{\prime}
\end{aligned}
$$.

question:
热核爆炸中火球的瞬时温度达 $10^{7} \mathrm{~K}$. 求:
(1) 辐射最强的波长;
(2) 这种波长的能量子 $h \nu$ 是多少?

The instantaneous temperature of the fireball in a thermonuclear explosion reaches $10^{7} \mathrm{~K}$. Find:  
(1) The wavelength at which radiation is strongest;  
(2) What is the energy quantum $h \nu$ of this wavelength?

solution:
要制造用可见光工作的光电池，必须选用功函数值低于可见光光子能量的材料。取可见光波长 $\lambda=0.4 \sim 0.8 \mu \mathrm{~m}$ ，相应的光子最小能量和最大能量分别为

$$
\begin{aligned}
E_{\min } & =h \nu_{\min }=h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\max }} \\
& =6.626 \times 10^{-34} \mathrm{~J} \cdot \mathrm{~s} \times \frac{3 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}}{0.8 \mu \mathrm{~m}} \\
& =2.48 \times 10^{-9} \mathrm{~J}=1.6 \mathrm{eV} \\
E_{\max } & =h \nu_{\max }=h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\min }}=2 h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\min }}=3.1 \mathrm{eV}
\end{aligned}
$$

即可见光的光子能量为 $1.6 \sim 3.1 \mathrm{eV}$. 可见，在已知的几种材料中，只能选用钢或锂作为光电池的材料。

To manufacture a photovoltaic cell that operates with visible light, one must select a material with a work function lower than the energy of visible light photons. Given the visible light wavelength $\lambda=0.4 \sim 0.8 \mu \mathrm{~m}$, the corresponding minimum and maximum photon energies are:

$$
\begin{aligned}
E_{\min } & =h \nu_{\min }=h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\max }} \\
& =6.626 \times 10^{-34} \mathrm{~J} \cdot \mathrm{~s} \times \frac{3 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}}{0.8 \mu \mathrm{~m}} \\
& =2.48 \times 10^{-9} \mathrm{~J}=1.6 \mathrm{eV} \\
E_{\max } & =h \nu_{\max }=h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\min }}=2 h \frac{c}{\lambda_{\min }}=3.1 \mathrm{eV}
\end{aligned}
$$

Thus, the photon energy of visible light is $1.6 \sim 3.1 \mathrm{eV}$. It is evident that, among the known materials, only steel or lithium can be selected as the material for the photovoltaic cell.

