解 两端固定，弦长 $l$ 与波长有关系为
$$
l=n \cdot \frac{\lambda_{n}}{2}, \quad v_{n}=\frac{v}{\lambda_{n}}=n \frac{v}{2 l}
$$
不按手指演奏的是基频，
$$
v_{1}=\frac{v}{2 l}=440 \mathrm{~Hz}
$$
按手指使琴弦长度缩短，奏出的仍是基频，
$$
\begin{gathered}
v_{l}^{\prime}=\frac{v}{2 l^{\prime}}, \quad \frac{v_{1}^{\prime}}{v_{1}}=\frac{l}{l^{\prime}} \\ l^{\prime}=\frac{v_{1}}{v_{1}^{\prime}} l=\frac{440}{528} \times 0.50=0.417(\mathrm{~m})
\end{gathered}
$$
离较近一端的距离
$$
\begin{gathered}
l-l^{\prime}=0.50-0.417=0.083(\mathrm{~m}) \\ v=\sqrt{\frac{T}{\eta}}, \quad v=2 l v_{1}, \quad \eta=\frac{m}{l} \\ T=\eta v^{2}=\frac{m}{l} \cdot\left(2 l v_{1}\right)^{2}=4 m l v_{1}^{2}=4 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-3} \times 0.50 \times(440)^{2}=774(\mathrm{~N})
\end{gathered}
$$

Solve the relationship between the length of a string with both ends fixed, length $l$, and wavelength:

$$
l=n \cdot \frac{\lambda_{n}}{2}, \quad v_{n}=\frac{v}{\lambda_{n}}=n \frac{v}{2 l}
$$

Not pressing the finger plays the fundamental frequency,

$$
v_{1}=\frac{v}{2 l}=440 \mathrm{~Hz}
$$

Pressing the finger shortens the string length, and the fundamental frequency is still played,

$$
\begin{gathered}
v_{l}^{\prime}=\frac{v}{2 l^{\prime}}, \quad \frac{v_{1}^{\prime}}{v_{1}}=\frac{l}{l^{\prime}} \\ l^{\prime}=\frac{v_{1}}{v_{1}^{\prime}} l=\frac{440}{528} \times 0.50=0.417(\mathrm{~m})
\end{gathered}
$$

The distance from the closer end is

$$
\begin{gathered}
l-l^{\prime}=0.50-0.417=0.083(\mathrm{~m}) \\ v=\sqrt{\frac{T}{\eta}}, \quad v=2 l v_{1}, \quad \eta=\frac{m}{l} \\ T=\eta v^{2}=\frac{m}{l} \cdot\left(2 l v_{1}\right)^{2}=4 m l v_{1}^{2}=4 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-3} \times 0.50 \times(440)^{2}=774(\mathrm{~N})
\end{gathered}
$$

解 两颗卫星沿同一椭圆轨道运动, 周期相同, 两颗卫星间的航程所需时间 $\Delta t$ 是不变的.

在近地点, 设 $M_{1} M_{2}$ 的中点的速率为 $v_{1}$, 两颗卫星 $M_{1} 、 M_{2}$ 相距不远, 都在近地点附近, 可认为这一段的速率近似为 $v_{1}$, 故有

$$
v_{1} \Delta t=b
$$

在远地点, 速率为 $v_{2}, M_{1} 、 M_{2}$ 相距为 $v_{2} \Delta t$, 因为

$$
\begin{gathered}
v_{1} R_{1}=v_{2} R_{2}, v_{2}=\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} v_{1} \\
M_{1} M_{2}=v_{2} \Delta t=\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} v_{1} \Delta t=\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} b
\end{gathered}
$$

在任意点 $\varphi$, 要算出在此点的速率 $v$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
& r=\frac{p}{1+e \cos \varphi} \\
& \dot{r}=\frac{p e \sin \varphi}{(1+e \cos \varphi)^{2}} \dot{\varphi}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
v^{2} & =\dot{r}^{2}+r^{2} \dot{\varphi}^{2}=\frac{p^{2} e^{2} \sin ^{2} \varphi}{(1+e \cos \varphi)^{4}} \dot{\varphi}^{2}+\frac{p^{2}}{(1+e \cos \varphi)^{2}} \dot{\varphi}^{2} \\
& =\frac{p^{2} \dot{\varphi}^{2}}{(1+e \cos \varphi)^{4}}\left(1+e^{2}+2 e \cos \varphi\right) \\
& =\frac{r^{4} \dot{\varphi}^{2}}{p^{2}}\left(1+e^{2}+2 e \cos \varphi\right)=\frac{h^{2}}{p^{2}}\left(1+e^{2}+2 e \cos \varphi\right) \\
v & =\frac{h}{p} \sqrt{1+e^{2}+2 e \cos \varphi}
\end{aligned}
$$

将 $h 、 p 、 e$ 用 $v_{1} 、 R_{1}$ 和 $R_{2}$ 表示,

$$
h=v_{1} R_{1}, \quad R_{1}=\frac{p}{1+e}, \quad R_{2}=\frac{p}{1-e}
$$

可得

$$
\begin{gathered}
e=\frac{R_{2}-R_{1}}{R_{1}+R_{2}}, p=\frac{2 R_{1} R_{2}}{R_{1}+R_{2}} \\
v=\frac{v_{1}}{2 R_{2}} \sqrt{2\left[R_{1}^{2}+R_{2}^{2}+\left(R_{2}^{2}-R_{1}^{2}\right) \cos \varphi\right]} \\
M_{1} M_{2}=v \Delta t=\frac{b}{2 R_{2}} \sqrt{2\left[R_{1}^{2}+R_{2}^{2}+\left(R_{2}^{2}-R_{1}^{2}\right) \cos \varphi\right]}
\end{gathered}
$$

可以验证：当 $\varphi=0$ 时， $M_{1} M_{2}=b$ ；当 $\varphi=\pi$ 时， $M_{1} M_{2}=\frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} b$ 。正是上述在近日点和远日点的两个结果。

Solve: Two satellites move along the same elliptical orbit with the same period. The travel time $\Delta t$ between the two satellites is constant.

At the periapsis, let the speed at the midpoint of $M_{1} M_{2}$ be $v_{1}$. The two satellites $M_{1}$ and $M_{2}$ are not far apart and are near the periapsis, so the speed in this segment can be approximated as $v_{1}$. Therefore, we have

$$
v_{1} \Delta t = b
$$

At the apoapsis, the speed is $v_{2}$, and the distance between $M_{1}$ and $M_{2}$ is $v_{2} \Delta t$. Because

$$
\begin{gathered}
v_{1} R_{1} = v_{2} R_{2}, \quad v_{2} = \frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} v_{1} \\
M_{1} M_{2} = v_{2} \Delta t = \frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} v_{1} \Delta t = \frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} b
\end{gathered}
$$

At any point $\varphi$, we need to calculate the speed $v$ at this point.

$$
\begin{aligned}
& r = \frac{p}{1 + e \cos \varphi} \\
& \dot{r} = \frac{p e \sin \varphi}{(1 + e \cos \varphi)^{2}} \dot{\varphi}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
v^{2} & = \dot{r}^{2} + r^{2} \dot{\varphi}^{2} = \frac{p^{2} e^{2} \sin^{2} \varphi}{(1 + e \cos \varphi)^{4}} \dot{\varphi}^{2} + \frac{p^{2}}{(1 + e \cos \varphi)^{2}} \dot{\varphi}^{2} \\
& = \frac{p^{2} \dot{\varphi}^{2}}{(1 + e \cos \varphi)^{4}} \left(1 + e^{2} + 2 e \cos \varphi\right) \\
& = \frac{r^{4} \dot{\varphi}^{2}}{p^{2}} \left(1 + e^{2} + 2 e \cos \varphi\right) = \frac{h^{2}}{p^{2}} \left(1 + e^{2} + 2 e \cos \varphi\right) \\
v & = \frac{h}{p} \sqrt{1 + e^{2} + 2 e \cos \varphi}
\end{aligned}
$$

Express $h$, $p$, and $e$ in terms of $v_{1}$, $R_{1}$, and $R_{2}$,

$$
h = v_{1} R_{1}, \quad R_{1} = \frac{p}{1 + e}, \quad R_{2} = \frac{p}{1 - e}
$$

We can obtain

$$
\begin{gathered}
e = \frac{R_{2} - R_{1}}{R_{1} + R_{2}}, \quad p = \frac{2 R_{1} R_{2}}{R_{1} + R_{2}} \\
v = \frac{v_{1}}{2 R_{2}} \sqrt{2 \left[R_{1}^{2} + R_{2}^{2} + \left(R_{2}^{2} - R_{1}^{2}\right) \cos \varphi\right]} \\
M_{1} M_{2} = v \Delta t = \frac{b}{2 R_{2}} \sqrt{2 \left[R_{1}^{2} + R_{2}^{2} + \left(R_{2}^{2} - R_{1}^{2}\right) \cos \varphi\right]}
\end{gathered}
$$

It can be verified: when $\varphi = 0$, $M_{1} M_{2} = b$; when $\varphi = \pi$, $M_{1} M_{2} = \frac{R_{1}}{R_{2}} b$. These are exactly the two results at the periapsis and apoapsis mentioned above.

