question:
Using sodium light $5893 \AA$, Michelson interference fringes are observed. Initially, there are 12 bright rings in the interference field, and the center is bright. After moving the plane mirror $M_{1}$, the center swallows (or emits) 10 rings, and at this time, there are still 5 bright rings left in the interference field. Find:

(1) The distance that $M_{1}$ has moved;
(2) The interference order of the central bright spot at the beginning;
(3) The interference order of the 5th bright ring from the center after $M_{1}$ has moved.

solution:
解 由柯西公式 $n=A+B / \lambda^{2}$, 将 $\lambda_{1}=4000 \AA, n_{1}=1.63, \lambda_{2}=5000 \AA, n_{2}=1.58$ 代人上式,得
$$
\begin{aligned}
& 1.63=A+\frac{B}{4000^{2}} \\
& 1.58=A+\frac{B}{5000^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
解此二式, 得 $A=1.5, B=2.22 \times 10^{6} \AA^{2}$. 由柯西公式, 有 $\frac{\mathrm{d} n}{\mathrm{~d} \lambda}=-\frac{2 B}{\lambda^{2}}$, 将 $A 、 B$ 值及 $\lambda=6000 \AA$ 代人, 得
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d} n}{\mathrm{~d} \lambda} & =-\frac{2 \times 2.22 \times 10^{6}}{(6000)^{3}}=-2.06 \times 10^{-5}(/ \AA) \\
& =-2.06 \times 10^{3}(/ \mathrm{cm})
\end{aligned}
$$

Solve using Cauchy's formula $n=A+B / \lambda^{2}$, substitute $\lambda_{1}=4000 \AA, n_{1}=1.63, \lambda_{2}=5000 \AA, n_{2}=1.58$ into the equation, we get
$$
\begin{aligned}
& 1.63=A+\frac{B}{4000^{2}} \\
& 1.58=A+\frac{B}{5000^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
Solving these two equations, we obtain $A=1.5, B=2.22 \times 10^{6} \AA^{2}$. According to Cauchy's formula, we have $\frac{\mathrm{d} n}{\mathrm{~d} \lambda}=-\frac{2 B}{\lambda^{2}}$, substitute the values of $A$, $B$ and $\lambda=6000 \AA$, we get
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\mathrm{d} n}{\mathrm{~d} \lambda} & =-\frac{2 \times 2.22 \times 10^{6}}{(6000)^{3}}=-2.06 \times 10^{-5}(/ \AA) \\
& =-2.06 \times 10^{3}(/ \mathrm{cm})
\end{aligned}
$$.

（1）设球面的半径为 $R$, 则根据对称性和高斯定理得均匀球面电荷产生的电场强度为
球内:
球外：
$$
\begin{aligned}
\boldsymbol{E} & =0 \\
\boldsymbol{E} & =\frac{e \boldsymbol{r}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} r^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
于是得静电能量为
$$
\begin{aligned}
W & =\frac{1}{2} \iiint \boldsymbol{E} \cdot \boldsymbol{D} \mathrm{d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2} \iiint E^{2} \mathrm{~d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2}\left(\frac{e}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}}\right)^{2} \int_{R}^{\infty} \frac{4 \pi r^{2} \mathrm{~d} r}{r^{4}} \\
& =\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \int_{R}^{\infty} \frac{\mathrm{d} r}{r^{2}}=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=m \varepsilon^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$
故得电子的半径为
$$
R=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} m \varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{1}{2} \frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}
$$
（2）设球体的半径为 $R$ ，由于电荷是均匀分布的，故球外的静电能量仍为式（3）。只须求球内的静电能量. 由对称性和高斯定理得, 球内离球心为 $r$ 处电场强度为
$$
\boldsymbol{E}=\frac{e \boldsymbol{r}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{3}}
$$
式中 $r$ 是球心到场点的位矢, $r=|r|$. 球内的静电能量为
$$
W_{i}=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2} \iiint E^{2} \mathrm{~d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2}\left(\frac{e}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{3}}\right)^{2} \int_{0}^{R} r^{2} \cdot 4 \pi r^{2} \mathrm{~d} r=\frac{e^{2}}{40 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}
$$
于是得总静电能量为
$$
W=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}+\frac{e^{2}}{40 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=\frac{3 e^{2}}{20 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=m \varepsilon^{2}
$$
故得电子的半径为
$$
R=\frac{3 e^{2}}{20 \pi \varepsilon_{0} m \varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{3}{5} \frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}
$$
（3）经典电子半径的值为
$$
\begin{aligned}
r_{e} & =\frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}=9.0 \times 10^{9} \times \frac{\left(1.6 \times 10^{-19}\right)^{2}}{9.1 \times 10^{-31} \times\left(3.0 \times 10^{8}\right)^{2}} \\
& =2.8 \times 10^{-15}(\mathrm{~m})=2.8(\mathrm{fm})
\end{aligned}
$$

(1) Let the radius of the sphere be $R$. According to symmetry and Gauss's theorem, the electric field intensity produced by a uniformly charged spherical surface is:

Inside the sphere:
Outside the sphere:
$$
\begin{aligned}
\boldsymbol{E} & =0 \\
\boldsymbol{E} & =\frac{e \boldsymbol{r}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} r^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
Thus, the electrostatic energy is given by
$$
\begin{aligned}
W & =\frac{1}{2} \iiint \boldsymbol{E} \cdot \boldsymbol{D} \mathrm{d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2} \iiint E^{2} \mathrm{~d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2}\left(\frac{e}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}}\right)^{2} \int_{R}^{\infty} \frac{4 \pi r^{2} \mathrm{~d} r}{r^{4}} \\
& =\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \int_{R}^{\infty} \frac{\mathrm{d} r}{r^{2}}=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=m \varepsilon^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$
Therefore, the radius of the electron is
$$
R=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} m \varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{1}{2} \frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}
$$
(2) Let the radius of the sphere be $R$. Since the charge is uniformly distributed, the electrostatic energy outside the sphere remains as in equation (3). We only need to calculate the electrostatic energy inside the sphere. By symmetry and Gauss's theorem, the electric field intensity at a distance $r$ from the center of the sphere is
$$
\boldsymbol{E}=\frac{e \boldsymbol{r}}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{3}}
$$
where $r$ is the position vector from the center to the point in question, $r=|r|$. The electrostatic energy inside the sphere is
$$
W_{i}=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2} \iiint E^{2} \mathrm{~d} V=\frac{\varepsilon_{0}}{2}\left(\frac{e}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{3}}\right)^{2} \int_{0}^{R} r^{2} \cdot 4 \pi r^{2} \mathrm{~d} r=\frac{e^{2}}{40 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}
$$
Thus, the total electrostatic energy is
$$
W=\frac{e^{2}}{8 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}+\frac{e^{2}}{40 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=\frac{3 e^{2}}{20 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=m \varepsilon^{2}
$$
Therefore, the radius of the electron is
$$
R=\frac{3 e^{2}}{20 \pi \varepsilon_{0} m \varepsilon^{2}}=\frac{3}{5} \frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}
$$
(3) The value of the classical electron radius is
$$
\begin{aligned}
r_{e} & =\frac{1}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0}} \frac{e^{2}}{m \varepsilon^{2}}=9.0 \times 10^{9} \times \frac{\left(1.6 \times 10^{-19}\right)^{2}}{9.1 \times 10^{-31} \times\left(3.0 \times 10^{8}\right)^{2}} \\
& =2.8 \times 10^{-15}(\mathrm{~m})=2.8(\mathrm{fm})
\end{aligned}
$$

（1）根据前面5.2.9 题，无穷大平面上的均匀电流 $\boldsymbol{k}$ 所产生的磁场是均匀磁场，其磁感强度 $\boldsymbol{B}$ 为

$$
\boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k} \times \boldsymbol{n}
$$

式中 $\boldsymbol{n}$ 是由电流面到场点的法线方向上的单位矢量, 故 $\boldsymbol{k}_{1}$ 和 $\boldsymbol{k}_{2}$ 在两面之间产生的磁感强度为

$$
\begin{aligned}
\boldsymbol{B} & =\boldsymbol{B}_{1}+\boldsymbol{B}_{2}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right) \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}-\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

式中 $\boldsymbol{n}_{12}$ 为电流面法线方向上的单位矢量, 由 $\boldsymbol{k}_{1}$ 指向 $\boldsymbol{k}_{2}, \boldsymbol{B}$ 的大小为

$$
\begin{aligned}
B & =\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}+2 B_{1} B_{2} \cos (\pi-\theta)}=\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}-2 B_{1} B_{2} \cos \theta} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \sqrt{k_{1}^{2}+k_{2}^{2}-2 k_{1} k_{2} \cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
$$

(2)两面之外的磁感强度

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \text { 外边: } \\
& \boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right)+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right) \\
& =-\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12} \\
& \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \text { 外边: } \\
& \boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

$\boldsymbol{B}$ 的大小都是

$$
\begin{aligned}
B & =\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}+2 B_{1} B \cos \theta} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \sqrt{k_{1}^{2}+k_{2}^{2}+2 k_{1} k_{2} \cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
$$

(3) 当 $\theta=\pi$, 且 $\left|\boldsymbol{k}_{1}\right|=\left|\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right|$ 时, 两面之间的磁感强度为

$$
\boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}-\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}=\mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
$$
两面之外的磁感强度为

$$
\boldsymbol{B}= \pm \frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}=0
$$

(1) According to the previous problem 5.2.9, the magnetic field produced by a uniform current $\boldsymbol{k}$ on an infinite plane is a uniform magnetic field, and its magnetic induction intensity $\boldsymbol{B}$ is

$$
\boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k} \times \boldsymbol{n}
$$

where $\boldsymbol{n}$ is the unit vector in the normal direction from the current plane to the field point. Therefore, the magnetic induction intensity produced by $\boldsymbol{k}_{1}$ and $\boldsymbol{k}_{2}$ between the two planes is

$$
\begin{aligned}
\boldsymbol{B} & =\boldsymbol{B}_{1}+\boldsymbol{B}_{2}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right) \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}-\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

where $\boldsymbol{n}_{12}$ is the unit vector in the normal direction of the current plane pointing from $\boldsymbol{k}_{1}$ to $\boldsymbol{k}_{2}$. The magnitude of $\boldsymbol{B}$ is

$$
\begin{aligned}
B & =\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}+2 B_{1} B_{2} \cos (\pi-\theta)}=\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}-2 B_{1} B_{2} \cos \theta} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \sqrt{k_{1}^{2}+k_{2}^{2}-2 k_{1} k_{2} \cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
$$

(2) The magnetic induction intensity outside the two planes

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \text{Outside } \boldsymbol{k}_{1}: \\
& \boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right)+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times\left(-\boldsymbol{n}_{12}\right) \\
& =-\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12} \\
& \text{Outside } \boldsymbol{k}_{2}: \\
& \boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}+\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{2} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
\end{aligned}
$$

The magnitude of $\boldsymbol{B}$ is

$$
\begin{aligned}
B & =\sqrt{B_{1}^{2}+B_{2}^{2}+2 B_{1} B_{2} \cos \theta} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0} \sqrt{k_{1}^{2}+k_{2}^{2}+2 k_{1} k_{2} \cos \theta}
\end{aligned}
$$

(3) When $\theta=\pi$, and $\left|\boldsymbol{k}_{1}\right|=\left|\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right|$, the magnetic induction intensity between the two planes is

$$
\boldsymbol{B}=\frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}-\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}=\mu_{0} \boldsymbol{k}_{1} \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}
$$

The magnetic induction intensity outside the two planes is

$$
\boldsymbol{B}= \pm \frac{1}{2} \mu_{0}\left(\boldsymbol{k}_{1}+\boldsymbol{k}_{2}\right) \times \boldsymbol{n}_{12}=0
$$

解 月球、地球质量分别记为 $m, M$ ，月球绕地球圆运动角速度记为 $\omega$, 则有
$$
\begin{aligned}
m \omega^{2} r & =\frac{G M m}{r^{2}} \\
r^{3} & =\frac{G M}{\omega^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
将
$$
G M=g R^{2}, \quad \omega=\frac{2 \pi}{T}
$$
代入，其中地球半径 $R$ 约为 $6.4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~km}$ ，月球绕地球旋转周期 $T$ 约为 $30 \mathrm{~d} （$ 天），可估算得
$$
r=\sqrt[3]{\frac{g R^{2} T^{2}}{4 \pi^{2}}} \sim 4.1 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m}=4.1 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~km}
$$
（ $T$ 实为 $27.3 \mathrm{~d}, r$ 约为 $3.8 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~km}$ ）。

Let the masses of the Moon and the Earth be denoted as $m$ and $M$, respectively, and let the angular velocity of the Moon's circular motion around the Earth be denoted as $\omega$. Then we have:

$$
\begin{aligned}
m \omega^{2} r & =\frac{G M m}{r^{2}} \\
r^{3} & =\frac{G M}{\omega^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Substitute

$$
G M=g R^{2}, \quad \omega=\frac{2 \pi}{T}
$$

where the radius of the Earth $R$ is approximately $6.4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~km}$, and the orbital period of the Moon around the Earth $T$ is approximately $30 \mathrm{~d}$ (days). We can estimate that

$$
r=\sqrt[3]{\frac{g R^{2} T^{2}}{4 \pi^{2}}} \sim 4.1 \times 10^{8} \mathrm{~m}=4.1 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~km}
$$

($T$ is actually $27.3 \mathrm{~d}$, $r$ is approximately $3.8 \times 10^{5} \mathrm{~km}$).

question:
一热气球的体积 $V=1.2 \mathrm{~m}^{3}$, 不可膨胀, 气球外壳的质量 $m=0.2 \mathrm{~kg}$, 其体积可以忽略不计. 当大气压强 $p_{0}=1.0 \mathrm{~atm}$ ，气温 $t_{1}=20^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ 时，气球恰好悬浮在地面上的大气中:
(1) 问气球内热空气的温度 $t_{2}$ 为多大? 设大气的摩尔分子量 $\mu=29 \mathrm{~g} / \mathrm{mol}$;
（2）先把气球系牢在地面上，将其内部空气加热到 $t_{2}=110^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ ，并保持恒定，然后释放气球. 若不考虑空气阻力, 求气球的初始加速度 $a$;
（3）若气球密封、绝热，保持温度 $t_{3}=110^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ ，在地面大气压强 $p_{0}=1.0 \mathrm{~atm}$ ，温度 $t_{1}=$ $20^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ 的等温大气中，气球可达到的稳定高度 $h$ 是多少?
