solution:
解 最小功分成两部分：一部分用来把 $25^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ 水冷却至 $0^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ ；另一部分用来实现水 $\rightarrow$ 冰相变。
$$
\begin{aligned}
& W_{1}=\int_{T_{0}}^{T_{1}} \frac{T_{0}-T}{T} M c_{p}(-\mathrm{d} T)=M c_{p} T_{0} \ln \frac{T_{0}}{T_{1}}-M c_{p}\left(T_{0}-T_{1}\right)=1.1 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal} \\
& W_{2}=\frac{T_{0}-T_{1}}{T_{1}} L M=7.3 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal}
\end{aligned}
$$
故至少需要做功
$$
W=W_{1}+W_{2}=8.4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal}=35 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~J}
$$

The minimum work is divided into two parts: one part is used to cool the water from $25^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ to $0^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$; the other part is used for the water $\rightarrow$ ice phase transition.
$$
\begin{aligned}
& W_{1}=\int_{T_{0}}^{T_{1}} \frac{T_{0}-T}{T} M c_{p}(-\mathrm{d} T)=M c_{p} T_{0} \ln \frac{T_{0}}{T_{1}}-M c_{p}\left(T_{0}-T_{1}\right)=1.1 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal} \\
& W_{2}=\frac{T_{0}-T_{1}}{T_{1}} L M=7.3 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal}
\end{aligned}
$$
Therefore, the minimum work required is
$$
W=W_{1}+W_{2}=8.4 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{cal}=35 \times 10^{3} \mathrm{~J}
$$.

question:
链有 $N$ 个节, 只能从一端打开, 即只有前面的 $s-1$ 个节相继打开后, 第 $s$ 节才能打开. 每个节闭合时能量为零, 打开时能量为 $\varepsilon$. 这是一种表示两股不交缠 DNA 分子的简单模型. 试求:
(1) 拉链的配分函数;
(2) 当 $\varepsilon>k T$ 时, 开节的平均数. $T$ 为拉链的温度.

The chain has $N$ links and can only be opened from one end, meaning that only after the first $s-1$ links are successively opened can the $s$-th link be opened. Each link has zero energy when closed and energy $\varepsilon$ when opened. This is a simple model representing two non-intertwined DNA molecules. Try to find:
(1) The partition function of the zipper;
(2) The average number of open links when $\varepsilon > k T$, where $T$ is the temperature of the zipper.

solution:
解 对于单个原子
$$
\begin{gathered}
\varepsilon=-\frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}-\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}} \\
\bar{\varepsilon}^{2}=\frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}
\end{gathered}
$$
对于两个原子
$$
\begin{aligned}
& E=\bar{\varepsilon}_{1}+\bar{\varepsilon}_{2}=-2 \frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}-\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}} \\
& \overline{E^{2}}=\overline{\left(\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2}\right)^{2}}=\overline{\varepsilon_{1}^{2}}+\overline{\varepsilon_{2}^{2}}+\overline{2 \varepsilon_{1} \varepsilon_{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
因为
$$
\overline{\varepsilon_{1} \varepsilon_{2}}=\overline{\varepsilon_{1}} \cdot \overline{\varepsilon_{2}}
$$
所以
$$
\overline{E^{2}}=2 \frac{2\left(\mathrm{e}^{2 \beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-2 \beta}\right)+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{\left(1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}\right)^{2}}
$$

Solution for a single atom
$$
\begin{gathered}
\varepsilon=-\frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}-\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}} \\
\bar{\varepsilon}^{2}=\frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}
\end{gathered}
$$
For two atoms
$$
\begin{aligned}
& E=\bar{\varepsilon}_{1}+\bar{\varepsilon}_{2}=-2 \frac{\mathrm{e}^{\beta}-\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}} \\
& \overline{E^{2}}=\overline{\left(\varepsilon_{1}+\varepsilon_{2}\right)^{2}}=\overline{\varepsilon_{1}^{2}}+\overline{\varepsilon_{2}^{2}}+\overline{2 \varepsilon_{1} \varepsilon_{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$
Because
$$
\overline{\varepsilon_{1} \varepsilon_{2}}=\overline{\varepsilon_{1}} \cdot \overline{\varepsilon_{2}}
$$
Therefore
$$
\overline{E^{2}}=2 \frac{2\left(\mathrm{e}^{2 \beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-2 \beta}\right)+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}}{\left(1+\mathrm{e}^{\beta}+\mathrm{e}^{-\beta}\right)^{2}}
$$

