solution:
解 理想顺磁体的物态方程为 $\frac{M}{V}=\frac{c H}{T}$ ( $M$ 为顺磁体的磁矩),
$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{d} Q=\mathrm{d} U+\mathrm{d} W=\mathrm{d} U-\mu_{0} H \mathrm{~d} M, \quad C_{M}=\left(\frac{\partial Q}{\partial T}\right)_{M}=\left(\frac{\partial U}{\partial T}\right)_{M}, \mathrm{~d} U=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T \\
\mathrm{~d} Q=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T-\mu_{0} H \mathrm{~d} M, \mathrm{~d} M=\frac{c}{T} \mathrm{~d} H-\frac{c H}{T^{2}} \mathrm{~d} T \\
\mathrm{~d} Q=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T-\frac{\mu_{0} c H}{T} \mathrm{~d} H+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}} \mathrm{~d} T=\left(C_{M}+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}}\right) \mathrm{d} T-\frac{\mu_{0} c H}{T} \mathrm{~d} H \\
C_{H}=\left(\frac{\partial Q}{\partial T}\right)_{H}=C_{M}+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}} \\
C_{H}-C_{M}=\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}}=\frac{\mu_{0} M^{2}}{c}=\frac{\mu_{0} M H}{T}
\end{gathered}
$$

Solve the equation of state for an ideal paramagnet as $\frac{M}{V}=\frac{c H}{T}$ (where $M$ is the magnetic moment of the paramagnet),

$$
\begin{gathered}
\mathrm{d} Q=\mathrm{d} U+\mathrm{d} W=\mathrm{d} U-\mu_{0} H \mathrm{~d} M, \quad C_{M}=\left(\frac{\partial Q}{\partial T}\right)_{M}=\left(\frac{\partial U}{\partial T}\right)_{M}, \mathrm{~d} U=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T \\
\mathrm{~d} Q=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T-\mu_{0} H \mathrm{~d} M, \mathrm{~d} M=\frac{c}{T} \mathrm{~d} H-\frac{c H}{T^{2}} \mathrm{~d} T \\
\mathrm{~d} Q=C_{M} \mathrm{~d} T-\frac{\mu_{0} c H}{T} \mathrm{~d} H+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}} \mathrm{~d} T=\left(C_{M}+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}}\right) \mathrm{d} T-\frac{\mu_{0} c H}{T} \mathrm{~d} H \\
C_{H}=\left(\frac{\partial Q}{\partial T}\right)_{H}=C_{M}+\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}} \\
C_{H}-C_{M}=\frac{\mu_{0} c H^{2}}{T^{2}}=\frac{\mu_{0} M^{2}}{c}=\frac{\mu_{0} M H}{T}
\end{gathered}
$$.

解 均匀电场每一点强度 $\boldsymbol{E}_{0}$ 相同，其电场线为平行直线。选空间任一点为原点，并设该点上的电势为 $\varphi_{0}$ ，由（1.4）式求得任一点 $P$ 处的电势
$$
\begin{aligned}
\varphi(P) & =\varphi_{0}-\int_{0}^{P} \boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \mathrm{~d} \boldsymbol{l}=\varphi_{0}-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \int_{0}^{P} \mathrm{~d} \boldsymbol{l} \\
& =\varphi_{0}-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \boldsymbol{x}
\end{aligned}
$$

$\boldsymbol{x}$ 为 $P$ 点的位矢. 注意均匀电场可以看作由无穷大平行板电容器产生, 其电荷分布不在有限区域内，因此不能选 $\varphi(\infty)=0$ 。若选 $\varphi_{0}=0$ ，则有
$$
\varphi=-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \boldsymbol{x}
$$

To solve: In a uniform electric field, the strength at every point is the same, denoted as $\boldsymbol{E}_{0}$, and its field lines are parallel straight lines. Choose any point in space as the origin and set the potential at this point as $\varphi_{0}$. According to equation (1.4), find the potential at any point $P$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\varphi(P) & =\varphi_{0}-\int_{0}^{P} \boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \mathrm{~d} \boldsymbol{l}=\varphi_{0}-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \int_{0}^{P} \mathrm{~d} \boldsymbol{l} \\
& =\varphi_{0}-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \boldsymbol{x}
\end{aligned}
$$

where $\boldsymbol{x}$ is the position vector of point $P$. Note that a uniform electric field can be considered as being produced by an infinitely large parallel plate capacitor, whose charge distribution is not within a finite region, thus we cannot choose $\varphi(\infty)=0$. If we set $\varphi_{0}=0$, then:

$$
\varphi=-\boldsymbol{E}_{0} \cdot \boldsymbol{x}
$$

question:
Consider two linearly polarized plane waves with the same amplitude, the same polarization direction, and frequencies of $\omega+\mathrm{d} \omega$ and $\omega-\mathrm{d} \omega$, respectively, both propagating along the $z$-axis direction.  
(1) Find the resultant wave and prove that the amplitude of the wave is not constant, but a wave;  
(2) Determine the phase velocity and amplitude velocity of the resultant wave.

solution:
$$
\begin{gathered}
E_{x}=A_{1} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi}{b} y\right) \mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i} k_{x} x-\omega t)} \\
E_{y}=A_{2} \cos \left(\frac{n \pi}{b} y\right) \mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i} k_{y} x-\omega t)} \\
E_{x}=A_{3} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi}{b} y\right) \mathrm{e}^{\mathrm{i} k_{x} x-\omega t)} \\
k_{x}^{2}=\frac{\omega^{2}}{c^{2}}-\left(\frac{n \pi}{b}\right)^{2} \\
\frac{n \pi}{b} A_{3}=\mathrm{i} k_{x} A_{3}, \quad A_{1} \text{ is independent } \\
\text{ Cutoff frequency } \omega_{c}=\frac{n \pi c}{b}
\end{gathered}
$$.

