$$.

解: 角动量守恒定律，有心力。
在水平面内，小球只受到绳子的拉力的作用，这个拉力一直通过小孔，所以是个有心力，因此这个力对小孔的力矩一直为零，所以小球对小孔的角动量守恒，而且这个拉力提供小球作圆周运动的向心力，因此有
$$
\begin{gathered}
m v_{1} r_{1}=m v_{2} r_{2} \\
v_{2}=\frac{r_{1}}{r_{2}} v_{1}
\end{gathered}
$$
所以小球动能的增量为
$$
\Delta E_{k}=\frac{1}{2} m v_{2}^{2}-\frac{1}{2} m v_{1}^{2}=\frac{1}{2} m\left(v_{2}^{2}-v_{1}^{2}\right)=\frac{1}{2} m v_{1}^{2} \frac{r_{1}^{2}-r_{2}^{2}}{r_{2}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2} m \omega_{1}^{2} r_{1}^{2} \frac{r_{1}^{2}-r_{2}^{2}}{r_{2}^{2}}
$$

Solution: Conservation of angular momentum, central force. In the horizontal plane, the ball is only subjected to the tension of the string, which always passes through the small hole, so it is a central force. Therefore, the torque of this force about the small hole is always zero, so the angular momentum of the ball about the small hole is conserved. This tension provides the centripetal force for the ball's circular motion, thus

$$
\begin{gathered}
m v_{1} r_{1} = m v_{2} r_{2} \\
v_{2} = \frac{r_{1}}{r_{2}} v_{1}
\end{gathered}
$$

Therefore, the increment in the kinetic energy of the ball is

$$
\Delta E_{k} = \frac{1}{2} m v_{2}^{2} - \frac{1}{2} m v_{1}^{2} = \frac{1}{2} m\left(v_{2}^{2} - v_{1}^{2}\right) = \frac{1}{2} m v_{1}^{2} \frac{r_{1}^{2} - r_{2}^{2}}{r_{2}^{2}} = \frac{1}{2} m \omega_{1}^{2} r_{1}^{2} \frac{r_{1}^{2} - r_{2}^{2}}{r_{2}^{2}}
$$

高斯定理，电场强度。关于题目中 "距离球面 $R$ 处" 个人认为表述上不太严谨，一则没有说明球内还是球外，二则到一个曲面的距离要怎么定义？这里理解成半径为 $2 R$ 的球面。取半径为 $r=2 R$ 的球面为高斯面，由高斯定理，得
$$
\begin{gathered}
\oint_{S} \vec{E} \cdot \mathrm{~d} \vec{S}=E \cdot 4 \pi r^{2}=E \cdot 4 \pi(2 R)^{2}=16 \pi R^{2} E=\frac{q}{\varepsilon_{0}}=\frac{\sigma \cdot 4 \pi R^{2}}{\varepsilon_{0}} \\
E=\frac{\sigma}{4 \varepsilon_{0}}
\end{gathered}
$$

 Gauss's theorem, electric field intensity. Regarding the expression "at a distance $R$ from the spherical surface" in the problem, I personally think it is not very precise. Firstly, it does not specify whether it is inside or outside the sphere, and secondly, how to define the distance to a surface? Here, it is understood as the spherical surface with a radius of $2R$. Taking a spherical surface with a radius of $r=2R$ as the Gaussian surface, according to Gauss's theorem, we have
$$
\begin{gathered}
\oint_{S} \vec{E} \cdot \mathrm{~d} \vec{S}=E \cdot 4 \pi r^{2}=E \cdot 4 \pi(2 R)^{2}=16 \pi R^{2} E=\frac{q}{\varepsilon_{0}}=\frac{\sigma \cdot 4 \pi R^{2}}{\varepsilon_{0}} \\
E=\frac{\sigma}{4 \varepsilon_{0}}
\end{gathered}
$$.

电势和电势能。
带电量为 $q$ 的点电荷置于电场中电势为 $V$ 处所具有的电势能为 $W$ ，则有
$$
\begin{aligned}
& W=q V \\
& V=\frac{W}{q}
\end{aligned}
$$
所以，电势在数值上等于单位正电荷在该处时的电势能。
而电场力做功，电势能减少，所以某处的电势能等于电荷从该处移到电势能零点时电场力所做的功。

Electric potential and electric potential energy. The electric potential energy of a point charge with charge $q$ placed at a point with electric potential $V$ in an electric field is $W$, thus:

$$
\begin{aligned}
& W=q V \\
& V=\frac{W}{q}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, numerically, the electric potential is equal to the electric potential energy at that point for a unit positive charge. When the electric field does work, the electric potential energy decreases, so the electric potential energy at a certain point is equal to the work done by the electric field when the charge moves from that point to the point where the electric potential energy is zero.

电场叠加原理。
如图，选择两个对称的电荷元，则它们在 $O$ 点的合场强沿 $y$ 轴负方向，即

$$
\mathrm{d} E_{y}=-2 \frac{\mathrm{~d} q}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \times \sin \theta=-\frac{\lambda R \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}=-\frac{\lambda \sin \theta \mathrm{d} \theta}{2 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=-\frac{Q \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}
$$

所以总场强为

$$
\begin{aligned}
E_{y}=\int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}-\frac{Q \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} & =-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}(-\cos \theta)_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}=-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \\
\vec{E} & =-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \vec{e}_{y}
\end{aligned}
$$

![img-283.jpeg](images/img-283.jpeg)

The principle of superposition of electric fields.

As shown in the figure, select two symmetrical charge elements, then their combined electric field at point $O$ is along the negative direction of the $y$-axis, i.e.,

$$
\mathrm{d} E_{y}=-2 \frac{\mathrm{~d} q}{4 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \times \sin \theta=-\frac{\lambda R \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}=-\frac{\lambda \sin \theta \mathrm{d} \theta}{2 \pi \varepsilon_{0} R}=-\frac{Q \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}
$$

Therefore, the total electric field is

$$
\begin{aligned}
E_{y}=\int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}-\frac{Q \sin \theta \mathrm{~d} \theta}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} & =-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}}(-\cos \theta)_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}=-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \\
\vec{E} & =-\frac{Q}{2 \pi^{2} \varepsilon_{0} R^{2}} \vec{e}_{y}
\end{aligned}
$$

