$$
E = -\frac{q}{4\pi\varepsilon_{0}}\Biggl[\frac{1}{r a} + \frac{1}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}} - \frac{r/a}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}}\Biggr]e_{z}
$$
如果 $q \to -q$，则有 $(0,0,-a)$ 处有最大的负感应电荷面密度，由上式可得所需 $Q$ 为：
$$
\begin{aligned}
Q &> -\sigma \cdot 4\pi a^{2} \\
&= -\varepsilon_{0} \cdot 4\pi a^{2} \left(\frac{-q}{4\pi\varepsilon_{0}}\right) \cdot \left[\frac{1}{r a} + \frac{1}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}} - \frac{r/a}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}}\right] \\
&= q\left[\frac{a}{r} + \frac{a^{2}}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}} - \frac{a r}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}}\right] \\
&= \frac{q a^{2}(3r+a)}{r\left(r+a\right)^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

At the point $(0,0,-a^{-})$, the electric field is:

$$
E = -\frac{q}{4\pi\varepsilon_{0}}\Biggl[\frac{1}{r a} + \frac{1}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}} - \frac{r/a}{\left(r+a\right)^{2}}\Biggr]e_{z}
$$

If $q \to -q$, then the maximum negative induced charge surface density is at $(0,0,-a)$. From the above equation, the required $Q$ is:

$$
